import Scry.Rules
import Text
/-!
# Scry.Models

**External function models** (`import Scry.Models`): what a call to a libc function or a
syscall wrapper does to taint and memory, written down once instead of being scattered
through the lowering and the taint rules.

The model table has three kinds of entry:

* **libc/syscall semantics** — `getenv`, `read`/`recv`, the `exec*` family, `system`,
  `popen`, the `printf`/`sprintf`/`snprintf` family, the `strcpy`/`strcat`/`memcpy`
  family, `malloc`/`calloc`/`realloc` and `free`. These are the calls whose effects a
  reader can reasonably expect a C taint tool to know.
* **base policy** — the sanitiser names the default rule pack trusts (`escape_shell`,
  `sanitize`, `sanitize_path`, …). They are models because a sanitiser is an effect on a
  value, not a rule-pack side table; putting them here makes the effect visible to tests
  and to any frontend. A model sanitiser is only applied when the pack names the
  function (`RulePack.trustsSanitiser`), so a pack that omits `sanitize` still gets the
  no-sanitiser behaviour.
* **pure/none** — calls such as `strlen` or `strcmp` that neither copy taint nor write
  memory. A model with an empty effect list is a claim that the call is **modelled as
  pure**, not a claim that the function is safe in general.

## Effects

| effect | meaning |
|---|---|
| `source ref` | the result or an argument is attacker-controlled (a written buffer, `getenv`'s result) |
| `sink arg class` | the value at `arg` reaches a dangerous operation; `class` selects the rule (`command`, `format`, `length`, `size`) |
| `sanitise ref` | the result or an argument is cleaned in place |
| `copy dst src` | the call copies `src`'s contents into the object `dst` points at (`strcpy`) |
| `copyArgs dst first` | the call formats every argument from `first` into `dst` (`sprintf`, `snprintf`) |
| `alloc size count` | the call returns a fresh object; `size`/`count` are the size argument positions when they exist |
| `free arg` | the call may free the object at `arg` |
| `unknown` | the effect is not known; this is the explicit fallback for an unmodelled external |

`copyArgs` exists because a format call has no single source: the destination receives a
mixture of the format and its variadic arguments. It expands to `arity - first` copy
pairs, so the taint layer can treat each argument as a source of the written object.

## Unknown is explicit

`Scry.modelOf` returns `Option Scry.FnModel`; `Scry.modelFor` returns the `unknown` model
for a name that is not in the table. `Scry.isUnknownModel` is the predicate the analysis
uses to keep an unmodelled external's result and memory effect unknown (and to warn)
rather than silently treating the call as pure. An external call is only "modelled as
pure" when it has an entry with an empty effect list.

## Model rules

A sink effect names a class, and a class maps to one rule id: `command-injection`,
`format-string`, `buffer-overflow` or `integer-overflow`. `Scry.RulePack.withModels`
appends the missing rule descriptors (with no source/sink/sanitiser entries of their own)
so a rule pack does not have to repeat them. The descriptors are metadata for SARIF and
for a finding's `rule` field; the sink facts come from the model table.
-/

-- ## Effects

/-- The dangerous operation a sink argument reaches. The class selects the rule that
owns the finding. -/
inductive Scry.SinkClass where
  /-- A command interpreter or a command argument (`system`, `popen`, `exec*`). -/
  | command
  /-- A format string (`printf`, `sprintf`, `snprintf`). -/
  | format
  /-- A copy/read length or destination bound (`read`, `recv`, `snprintf`). -/
  | length
  /-- An allocation size (`malloc`, `calloc`, `realloc`). -/
  | size

def Scry.SinkClass.show : Scry.SinkClass → String
  | .command => "command"
  | .format => "format"
  | .length => "length"
  | .size => "size"

def Scry.SinkClass.ruleId : Scry.SinkClass → String
  | .command => "command-injection"
  | .format => "format-string"
  | .length => "buffer-overflow"
  | .size => "integer-overflow"

def Scry.SinkClass.severity : Scry.SinkClass → Scry.Severity
  | .command => .error
  | .format => .warning
  | .length => .warning
  | .size => .warning

def Scry.SinkClass.message : Scry.SinkClass → String
  | .command => "Attacker-controlled data reaches a command interpreter"
  | .format => "Attacker-controlled data is used as a format string"
  | .length => "Attacker-controlled length reaches a copy or read; the destination can overflow"
  | .size => "Attacker-controlled value reaches an allocation size; the size may overflow or exhaust memory"

/-- One effect of an external call. `ArgRef` is the rule pack's `result`/`arg K`
selector, so a model and a pack line mean the same thing. -/
/-- `copy dst src` writes `src`'s contents into the object `dst` points at;
`copyArgs dst first` writes the formatted arguments from `first` on into `dst`;
`alloc sizeArg countArg` returns a fresh object (the argument positions are optional,
so a format-driven allocation such as `asprintf` has neither); `free arg` frees the
object at `arg`; `unknown` is the explicit unmodelled fallback. -/
inductive Scry.Effect where
  | source (ref : Scry.ArgRef)
  | sink (arg : Nat) (sinkClass : Scry.SinkClass)
  | sanitise (ref : Scry.ArgRef)
  | copy (dst : Nat) (src : Nat)
  | copyArgs (dst : Nat) (first : Nat)
  | alloc (sizeArg : Option Nat) (countArg : Option Nat)
  | free (arg : Nat)
  | unknown

/-- The shape of an allocation effect. -/
structure Scry.AllocShape where
  sizeArg : Option Nat
  countArg : Option Nat

/-- One external function's model. `family` is descriptive (`libc`, `syscall`, `policy`,
`pure`); it is not consulted by the analysis. -/
structure Scry.FnModel where
  name : String
  family : String
  effects : List Scry.Effect
  note : String

-- ## Queries

def Scry.modelFlat {A B : Type} (f : A → List B) : List A → List B
  | .nil => .nil
  | .cons x xs => List.append (f x) (Scry.modelFlat f xs)

def Scry.modelSources (m : Scry.FnModel) : List Scry.ArgRef :=
  Scry.modelFlat (fun e => match e with
    | .source r => List.cons r .nil
    | _ => .nil) m.effects

def Scry.modelSans (m : Scry.FnModel) : List Scry.ArgRef :=
  Scry.modelFlat (fun e => match e with
    | .sanitise r => List.cons r .nil
    | _ => .nil) m.effects

def Scry.modelSinkArgs (m : Scry.FnModel) : List (Nat × Scry.SinkClass) :=
  Scry.modelFlat (fun e => match e with
    | .sink arg c => List.cons (arg, c) .nil
    | _ => .nil) m.effects

def Scry.modelRangeFrom : Nat → Nat → List Nat
  | .zero, _ => .nil
  | .succ k, first => List.append (Scry.modelRangeFrom k first)
      (List.cons (Nat.add first k) .nil)

/-- The `(destination, source)` pairs a model copies into. `arity` is the call's argument
count, which is what expands a `copyArgs` effect (a format call has no fixed arity). -/
def Scry.modelCopyPairs (m : Scry.FnModel) (arity : Nat) : List (Nat × Nat) :=
  Scry.modelFlat (fun e => match e with
    | .copy dst src => List.cons (dst, src) .nil
    | .copyArgs dst first => List.map (fun src => (dst, src))
        (Scry.modelRangeFrom (Nat.sub arity first) first)
    | _ => .nil) m.effects

def Scry.modelAlloc (m : Scry.FnModel) : Option Scry.AllocShape :=
  match List.find (fun e => match e with
    | .alloc _ _ => .true
    | _ => .false) m.effects with
  | .none => .none
  | .some e => match e with
    | .alloc sizeArg countArg => .some (Scry.AllocShape.mk sizeArg countArg)
    | _ => .none

def Scry.modelFreeArg (m : Scry.FnModel) : Option Nat :=
  match List.find (fun e => match e with
    | .free _ => .true
    | _ => .false) m.effects with
  | .none => .none
  | .some e => match e with
    | .free arg => .some arg
    | _ => .none

def Scry.modelHasUnknown (m : Scry.FnModel) : Bool :=
  List.any (fun e => match e with
    | .unknown => .true
    | _ => .false) m.effects

-- ## The table

def Scry.sourceGetenv : Scry.FnModel :=
  Scry.FnModel.mk "getenv" "libc" (List.cons (.source .result) .nil)
    "the environment value is attacker-controlled"

def Scry.sourceRead : Scry.FnModel :=
  Scry.FnModel.mk "read" "syscall"
    (List.cons (.source (.arg 1))
      (List.cons (.sink 2 .length) .nil))
    "fills buffer argument 1; the length argument 2 is a bound"

def Scry.sourceRecv : Scry.FnModel :=
  Scry.FnModel.mk "recv" "syscall"
    (List.cons (.source (.arg 1))
      (List.cons (.sink 2 .length) .nil))
    "fills buffer argument 1; the length argument 2 is a bound"

def Scry.sourceFgets : Scry.FnModel :=
  Scry.FnModel.mk "fgets" "libc" (List.cons (.source (.arg 0)) .nil)
    "fills buffer argument 0"

def Scry.sourceGetline : Scry.FnModel :=
  Scry.FnModel.mk "getline" "libc" (List.cons (.source (.arg 0)) .nil)
    "fills the line buffer argument 0"

def Scry.sourceFread : Scry.FnModel :=
  Scry.FnModel.mk "fread" "libc" (List.cons (.source (.arg 0)) .nil)
    "fills buffer argument 0"

def Scry.sinkSystem : Scry.FnModel :=
  Scry.FnModel.mk "system" "libc" (List.cons (.sink 0 .command) .nil)
    "argument 0 is passed to the shell"

def Scry.sinkPopen : Scry.FnModel :=
  Scry.FnModel.mk "popen" "libc" (List.cons (.sink 0 .command) .nil)
    "argument 0 is passed to the shell"

/-- `execl`/`execle`/`execlp` are variadic: the path is argument 0 and every argv entry
is a possible command argument. Positions 0–7 are modelled; a call with more arguments
is still handled by the lower-ranked positions, and the limit is stated here rather than
silently assuming one position. -/
def Scry.sinkExec : Scry.FnModel :=
  Scry.FnModel.mk "execl" "libc"
    (Scry.modelFlat (fun k => List.cons (.sink k .command) .nil)
      (Scry.modelRangeFrom 8 0))
    "path and every variadic argv entry are command sinks (positions 0–7)"

def Scry.sinkExeclp : Scry.FnModel :=
  Scry.FnModel.mk "execlp" "libc"
    (Scry.modelFlat (fun k => List.cons (.sink k .command) .nil)
      (Scry.modelRangeFrom 8 0))
    "path and every variadic argv entry are command sinks (positions 0–7)"

def Scry.sinkExecle : Scry.FnModel :=
  Scry.FnModel.mk "execle" "libc"
    (Scry.modelFlat (fun k => List.cons (.sink k .command) .nil)
      (Scry.modelRangeFrom 8 0))
    "path, argv and the environment are command sinks (positions 0–7)"

def Scry.sinkExecv : Scry.FnModel :=
  Scry.FnModel.mk "execv" "libc"
    (List.cons (.sink 0 .command) (List.cons (.sink 1 .command) .nil))
    "the path and the argv pointer"

def Scry.sinkExecvp : Scry.FnModel :=
  Scry.FnModel.mk "execvp" "libc"
    (List.cons (.sink 0 .command) (List.cons (.sink 1 .command) .nil))
    "the path and the argv pointer"

def Scry.sinkExecvpe : Scry.FnModel :=
  Scry.FnModel.mk "execvpe" "libc"
    (List.cons (.sink 0 .command)
      (List.cons (.sink 1 .command) (List.cons (.sink 2 .command) .nil)))
    "the path, the argv pointer and the environment"

def Scry.sinkExecve : Scry.FnModel :=
  Scry.FnModel.mk "execve" "libc"
    (List.cons (.sink 0 .command)
      (List.cons (.sink 1 .command) (List.cons (.sink 2 .command) .nil)))
    "the path, the argv pointer and the environment"

def Scry.sinkPosixSpawn : Scry.FnModel :=
  Scry.FnModel.mk "posix_spawn" "libc"
    (List.cons (.sink 1 .command)
      (List.cons (.sink 4 .command) (List.cons (.sink 5 .command) .nil)))
    "the path (1), argv (4) and environment (5); argument 0 is the pid output"

def Scry.sinkPosixSpawnp : Scry.FnModel :=
  Scry.FnModel.mk "posix_spawnp" "libc"
    (List.cons (.sink 1 .command)
      (List.cons (.sink 4 .command) (List.cons (.sink 5 .command) .nil)))
    "the path (1), argv (4) and environment (5); argument 0 is the pid output"

def Scry.sinkPrintf : Scry.FnModel :=
  Scry.FnModel.mk "printf" "libc" (List.cons (.sink 0 .format) .nil)
    "argument 0 is the format string"

def Scry.sinkFprintf : Scry.FnModel :=
  Scry.FnModel.mk "fprintf" "libc" (List.cons (.sink 1 .format) .nil)
    "argument 1 is the format string"

def Scry.sinkSprintf : Scry.FnModel :=
  Scry.FnModel.mk "sprintf" "libc"
    (List.cons (.sink 1 .format) (List.cons (.copyArgs 0 1) .nil))
    "argument 1 is the format; the formatted arguments are copied into the destination"

def Scry.sinkSnprintf : Scry.FnModel :=
  Scry.FnModel.mk "snprintf" "libc"
    (List.cons (.sink 1 .length)
      (List.cons (.sink 2 .format)
        (List.cons (.copyArgs 0 2) .nil)))
    "argument 1 is the bound, argument 2 the format; the formatted arguments are copied"

def Scry.sinkVprintf : Scry.FnModel :=
  Scry.FnModel.mk "vprintf" "libc" (List.cons (.sink 0 .format) .nil)
    "argument 0 is the format string"

def Scry.sinkVfprintf : Scry.FnModel :=
  Scry.FnModel.mk "vfprintf" "libc" (List.cons (.sink 1 .format) .nil)
    "argument 1 is the format string"

def Scry.sinkVsprintf : Scry.FnModel :=
  Scry.FnModel.mk "vsprintf" "libc"
    (List.cons (.sink 1 .format) (List.cons (.copyArgs 0 1) .nil))
    "argument 1 is the format; the formatted arguments are copied into the destination"

def Scry.sinkVsnprintf : Scry.FnModel :=
  Scry.FnModel.mk "vsnprintf" "libc"
    (List.cons (.sink 1 .length)
      (List.cons (.sink 2 .format)
        (List.cons (.copyArgs 0 2) .nil)))
    "argument 1 is the bound, argument 2 the format; the formatted arguments are copied"

def Scry.sinkSyslog : Scry.FnModel :=
  Scry.FnModel.mk "syslog" "libc" (List.cons (.sink 1 .format) .nil)
    "argument 1 is the format string"

def Scry.sinkDprintf : Scry.FnModel :=
  Scry.FnModel.mk "dprintf" "libc" (List.cons (.sink 1 .format) .nil)
    "argument 1 is the format string"

def Scry.copyStrcpy : Scry.FnModel :=
  Scry.FnModel.mk "strcpy" "libc" (List.cons (.copy 0 1) .nil)
    "argument 1 is copied into the object argument 0 points at"

def Scry.copyStrncpy : Scry.FnModel :=
  Scry.FnModel.mk "strncpy" "libc" (List.cons (.copy 0 1) .nil)
    "a bounded copy, still a copy from argument 1 to argument 0"

def Scry.copyStrcat : Scry.FnModel :=
  Scry.FnModel.mk "strcat" "libc" (List.cons (.copy 0 1) .nil)
    "argument 1 is appended to the object argument 0 points at"

def Scry.copyStrncat : Scry.FnModel :=
  Scry.FnModel.mk "strncat" "libc" (List.cons (.copy 0 1) .nil)
    "a bounded append, still a copy from argument 1 to argument 0"

def Scry.copyStpcpy : Scry.FnModel :=
  Scry.FnModel.mk "stpcpy" "libc" (List.cons (.copy 0 1) .nil)
    "argument 1 is copied into argument 0"

def Scry.copyStrlcpy : Scry.FnModel :=
  Scry.FnModel.mk "strlcpy" "libc" (List.cons (.copy 0 1) .nil)
    "a size-bounded copy from argument 1 to argument 0"

def Scry.copyStrlcat : Scry.FnModel :=
  Scry.FnModel.mk "strlcat" "libc" (List.cons (.copy 0 1) .nil)
    "a size-bounded append from argument 1 to argument 0"

def Scry.copyMemcpy : Scry.FnModel :=
  Scry.FnModel.mk "memcpy" "libc" (List.cons (.copy 0 1) .nil)
    "argument 1 is copied into argument 0"

def Scry.copyMemmove : Scry.FnModel :=
  Scry.FnModel.mk "memmove" "libc" (List.cons (.copy 0 1) .nil)
    "argument 1 is moved into argument 0"

def Scry.allocMalloc : Scry.FnModel :=
  Scry.FnModel.mk "malloc" "libc"
    (List.cons (.alloc (.some 0) .none) (List.cons (.sink 0 .size) .nil))
    "a fresh object; argument 0 is the byte count"

def Scry.allocCalloc : Scry.FnModel :=
  Scry.FnModel.mk "calloc" "libc"
    (List.cons (.alloc (.some 1) (.some 0))
      (List.cons (.sink 0 .size) (List.cons (.sink 1 .size) .nil)))
    "a fresh zeroed object; arguments 0 and 1 are the count and element size"

def Scry.allocRealloc : Scry.FnModel :=
  Scry.FnModel.mk "realloc" "libc"
    (List.cons (.alloc (.some 1) .none) (List.cons (.sink 1 .size) .nil))
    "a fresh object; the old object may also be freed (not modelled as a free here, to keep the may-alias result)"

def Scry.freeFree : Scry.FnModel :=
  Scry.FnModel.mk "free" "libc" (List.cons (.free 0) .nil)
    "argument 0 is freed"

-- Policy models: the sanitiser names the default pack trusts. A model supplies the
-- effect; the pack opts in by naming the function. The model is not a proof that the
-- function is safe for every use.

def Scry.sanEscapeShell : Scry.FnModel :=
  Scry.FnModel.mk "escape_shell" "policy" (List.cons (.sanitise .result) .nil)
    "shell-escapes its argument and returns a new string"

def Scry.sanShellescape : Scry.FnModel :=
  Scry.FnModel.mk "shellescape" "policy" (List.cons (.sanitise .result) .nil)
    "shell-escapes its argument and returns a new string"

def Scry.sanQuoteArg : Scry.FnModel :=
  Scry.FnModel.mk "quote_arg" "policy" (List.cons (.sanitise .result) .nil)
    "quotes one shell argument"

def Scry.sanSanitize : Scry.FnModel :=
  Scry.FnModel.mk "sanitize" "policy" (List.cons (.sanitise (.arg 0)) .nil)
    "cleans argument 0 in place"

def Scry.sanSanitizeFormat : Scry.FnModel :=
  Scry.FnModel.mk "sanitize_format" "policy" (List.cons (.sanitise .result) .nil)
    "returns a format string with no conversions"

def Scry.sanSanitizePath : Scry.FnModel :=
  Scry.FnModel.mk "sanitize_path" "policy" (List.cons (.sanitise .result) .nil)
    "returns a path with traversal components removed"

def Scry.sanConfinePath : Scry.FnModel :=
  Scry.FnModel.mk "confine_path" "policy" (List.cons (.sanitise .result) .nil)
    "confines a path to a base directory"

def Scry.sanCheckedSize : Scry.FnModel :=
  Scry.FnModel.mk "checked_size" "policy" (List.cons (.sanitise .result) .nil)
    "returns a size after an overflow check"

def Scry.sanClampLen : Scry.FnModel :=
  Scry.FnModel.mk "clamp_len" "policy" (List.cons (.sanitise .result) .nil)
    "returns a length clamped to a bound"

def Scry.sanClampSize : Scry.FnModel :=
  Scry.FnModel.mk "clamp_size" "policy" (List.cons (.sanitise .result) .nil)
    "returns a size clamped to a bound"

-- Pure/read-only calls: an empty effect list is a positive model, not `unknown`.
-- It says "this call does not copy attacker data, write memory or allocate"; the
-- analysis still keeps the argument's own register untainted (nothing is laundered).

def Scry.pureName (name : String) : Scry.FnModel :=
  Scry.FnModel.mk name "pure" .nil "modelled as pure: no taint, memory or allocation effect"

def Scry.pureModels : List Scry.FnModel :=
  List.map Scry.pureName
    [ "strlen", "strnlen", "strcmp", "strncmp", "strchr", "strrchr", "strstr"
    , "memcmp", "memchr", "atoi", "atol", "strtol", "strtoul", "strtod", "abs"
    , "isdigit", "isspace", "isalpha", "toupper", "tolower", "puts", "fputs"
    , "fwrite", "fflush", "close", "perror" ]

/-- A C#/CLR external call whose effect on the **value** is known: `result` is the
call's result type (`?` when unknown), `awaited` is what `await` yields for an async
call (`""` when the call is not async), and `note` states what the entry claims. A
listed call is `Scry.isModelled`, so the memory model does not report it as
`unmodelled-external`: the claim is only that the call affects its result and its
arguments by value (the C# rule pack still owns sources, sanitisers and sinks). A name
not in the table is unknown: its result type is `?` and its memory effect is warned
about with the name. -/
structure Scry.CsExternal where
  name : String
  result : String
  awaited : String
  note : String

/-- The C# value summary. These are the calls the lowerer emits for CLR/BCL code and
the ones a rule can propagate through; the table is deliberately small and every entry
names its effect. `""` in `awaited` means "not an async call"; `?` as a result means
"the value flows, its static type is not known". -/
def Scry.csExternals : List Scry.CsExternal :=
  [ Scry.CsExternal.mk "System.String.Concat" "System.String" ""
      "concatenates its arguments: taint flows to the result"
  , Scry.CsExternal.mk "System.String.Format" "System.String" ""
      "formats its arguments into the result"
  , Scry.CsExternal.mk "System.String.Join" "System.String" ""
      "joins its arguments into the result"
  , Scry.CsExternal.mk "System.String.Replace" "System.String" ""
      "replaces text; taint flows from the receiver and the arguments"
  , Scry.CsExternal.mk "System.String.Substring" "System.String" ""
      "a substring carries the receiver's taint"
  , Scry.CsExternal.mk "System.String.Trim" "System.String" ""
      "trims the receiver; taint flows"
  , Scry.CsExternal.mk "System.String.TrimStart" "System.String" ""
      "trims the receiver; taint flows"
  , Scry.CsExternal.mk "System.String.TrimEnd" "System.String" ""
      "trims the receiver; taint flows"
  , Scry.CsExternal.mk "System.String.ToUpper" "System.String" ""
      "changes case; taint flows"
  , Scry.CsExternal.mk "System.String.ToLower" "System.String" ""
      "changes case; taint flows"
  , Scry.CsExternal.mk "System.String.ToUpperInvariant" "System.String" ""
      "changes case; taint flows"
  , Scry.CsExternal.mk "System.String.ToLowerInvariant" "System.String" ""
      "changes case; taint flows"
  , Scry.CsExternal.mk "System.String.PadLeft" "System.String" ""
      "pads the receiver; taint flows"
  , Scry.CsExternal.mk "System.String.PadRight" "System.String" ""
      "pads the receiver; taint flows"
  , Scry.CsExternal.mk "System.String.Insert" "System.String" ""
      "inserts text; taint flows"
  , Scry.CsExternal.mk "System.String.Remove" "System.String" ""
      "removes text; taint flows"
  , Scry.CsExternal.mk "System.String.Split" "System.String[]" ""
      "splits the receiver; each part carries its taint"
  , Scry.CsExternal.mk "System.String.get_Length" "System.Int32" ""
      "a length is not tainted by the text's contents"
  , Scry.CsExternal.mk "System.String.StartsWith" "System.Boolean" ""
      "a predicate over the receiver"
  , Scry.CsExternal.mk "System.String.EndsWith" "System.Boolean" ""
      "a predicate over the receiver"
  , Scry.CsExternal.mk "System.String.Contains" "System.Boolean" ""
      "a predicate over the receiver"
  , Scry.CsExternal.mk "System.String.IndexOf" "System.Int32" ""
      "an index into the receiver"
  , Scry.CsExternal.mk "System.String.IsNullOrEmpty" "System.Boolean" ""
      "a predicate"
  , Scry.CsExternal.mk "System.String.IsNullOrWhiteSpace" "System.Boolean" ""
      "a predicate"
  , Scry.CsExternal.mk "System.Object.ToString" "System.String" ""
      "the receiver's text; taint flows from the receiver"
  , Scry.CsExternal.mk "System.Convert.ToString" "System.String" ""
      "converts its argument to text; taint flows"
  , Scry.CsExternal.mk "System.Int32.Parse" "System.Int32" ""
      "the rule pack owns the sanitiser; the result type is a number"
  , Scry.CsExternal.mk "System.Int64.Parse" "System.Int64" ""
      "the rule pack owns the sanitiser; the result type is a number"
  , Scry.CsExternal.mk "System.Guid.Parse" "System.Guid" ""
      "parses a GUID; the rule pack owns the sanitiser"
  , Scry.CsExternal.mk "System.IO.Path.Combine" "System.String" ""
      "joins path parts; taint flows to the result"
  , Scry.CsExternal.mk "System.IO.Path.GetFileName" "System.String" ""
      "selects a path component; taint flows"
  , Scry.CsExternal.mk "System.IO.Path.GetFileNameWithoutExtension" "System.String" ""
      "selects a path component; taint flows"
  , Scry.CsExternal.mk "System.IO.Path.GetExtension" "System.String" ""
